# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AIPLAY Studio — what never leaves this machine.
#
# This file is an ALLOW-LIST in spirit even though git only does deny-lists: the
# working tree contains tooling that talks to AIPLAY's own private dev server,
# and none of it belongs in a public repository. scripts/package.mjs enforces the
# same boundary for the distributable zip, and refuses to build if any of this
# reaches the staging tree. If you add a new private script, name it dev_* and it
# is excluded automatically.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ---- Private infrastructure. The important block. --------------------------
# 21 scripts that authenticate to and manipulate AIPLAY's dev server. They hold
# no literal secrets (credentials come from an external helper) but they map
# private infrastructure in detail.
scripts/dev_*
# The AIPLAY platform's own desktop feed endpoint — product code, not Studio.
dev-endpoint/
# The credentials helper itself, wherever it lands.
**/aiplay_creds*

# ---- Anything that could carry a secret -------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
settings.json          # the per-machine config: absolute paths, possibly tokens

# ---- Build output and dependencies ------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
*.tgz

# ---- Backups. `.bak-<tag>` is the convention used before every risky edit,
#      so these are numerous and always local. ------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej

# ---- Logs and scratch --------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.err
run.log
run.err
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# ---- Generated at runtime, not source ---------------------------------------
# Regenerate with: node scripts/export_workflows.mjs
# (kept OUT so the repo never disagrees with the graph builders)
workflows/*.json

# ---- Draft working material --------------------------------------------------
# Fact-check notes and superseded drafts, full of absolute local paths and
# corrections to text that has since been rewritten. The FINISHED docs live at
# the top of docs/; this is the scaffolding.
docs/_wf/

# ---- Internal handover notes -------------------------------------------------
# Written for whoever picks the work up next; full of local paths and half-formed
# decisions. Useful here, confusing in public.
CONTINUE_HERE.md

# ---- OS cruft ----------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---- One-off probes -----------------------------------------------------
# Scripts that answered a question once. The ANSWER lives in a comment in
# server/config.js; the script itself would just be 60 more files for a
# newcomer to triage. The measurement harnesses whose numbers are quoted in
# config.js are kept — a claim nobody can re-run is only an assertion.
